category: basics
position: 1
markdownify: false
---

<p>
  All of Attractive.js's built-in actions.
</p>

<p>
  Actions are declared via the <code>@action</code> attribute (or <code>@</code> for short).
</p>

<p>
  The <code>@target</code> attribute points to an element by its <code>id</code>. Use <code>@targets</code> for multiple elements via a CSS selector. If no target is given, the action runs on the element itself.
</p>

<ul class="no-content actions-list">
  <% Content::Action.all.in_order_of(:group, Content::Action::GROUPS).group_by { it.group }.each do |group, actions| %>
    <li class="group">
      <h2><%= group %></h2>

      <ul class="actions">
        <%= render actions %>
      </ul>
    </li>
  <% end%>
</ul>
